        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(reply): surface empty interactive completions",
        "body": "Closes #99712\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where an interactive direct turn could finish successfully with no assistant payload and no committed source reply, causing the user-facing channel turn to silently complete without any visible deliverable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDirect reply and queued follow-up delivery now share a bounded empty-interactive fallback that emits a visible error payload only when the run otherwise has no visible output. Existing silent paths remain silent for heartbeats, explicitly silent runs, message-tool-only delivery, and runs that already committed a message-tool, cron, approval, media, accepted child-session spawn, or other side-effect delivery.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers get a visible failure message when an interactive channel turn produces no deliverable output, instead of seeing the turn disappear. Message-tool-only, accepted child-session spawn, and known side-effect flows continue to avoid duplicate automatic replies.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: empty direct and follow-up interactive completions route a visible fallback while preserving silent/side-effect/message-tool-only exceptions, including accepted child-session spawn-only completions.\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - Head SHA: cbdf1217d602f19bbb5c8147ae2734262f9689e5\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner.misc.runreplyagent.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/followup-runner.test.ts` passed: 2 files, 151 tests.\n  - `git diff --check` passed.\n  - `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode local` exited 0 with `autoreview clean: no accepted/actionable findings reported`. The helper printed a Windows GBK decode thread exception after the clean result, but the command returned 0.\n- Observed result: focused tests cover main-run empty output, resolved `message_tool_only` suppression, follow-up empty fallback routing, source-delivered suppression, cron/approval suppression, compaction/progress paths that still finish with no visible final payload, and direct/follow-up acceptedSessionSpawns-only completions staying silent with no fallback routed.\n- Current-head CI proof: `Real behavior proof` passed on head cbdf1217d602f19bbb5c8147ae2734262f9689e5.\n- Not tested / proof gaps: no live Telegram Desktop proof was produced locally. The remaining real-channel proof requirement needs Mantis/maintainer-run Telegram proof or another redacted live channel artifact.",
